{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And upon the nobles of the children of Israel He did not lay His hand.</b> To remove them from their senses so that they would prophesy — as is the case with other prophets when the hand of HaShem is upon them, as it says in Ezekiel: וַתִּפֹּל עָלַי שָׁם יַד ה' (Ezekiel 8:1) — for then the activities of their senses cease, as happened to Saul when he prophesied, as it says: וַיִּפְשֹׁט גַּם הוּא בְּגָדָיו וַיִּתְנַבֵּא גַּם הוּא לִפְנֵי שְׁמוּאֵל וַיִּפֹּל עָרֹם כָּל הַיּוֹם הַהוּא וְכָל הַלָּיְלָה (1 Samuel 19:24). But these nobles — He did not lay His hand upon them to remove them from their senses, in order that they might grasp what they then saw." "<b>And they beheld the Elohim.</b> In a prophetic vision." "<b>And they ate and drank.</b> Afterward they held a feast without any change in their senses, and this they did in joy over what they had attained."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:08.469348080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}